# Guide

@"@voxgig/apidef/model/guide.aontu"

@"./base-guide.aontu"

# SENDING TAKES A BARE JSON ARRAY. Both send routes declare their request body
# as an array of SmsMessageRequest, but the generated create() input is a map
# (SendMessageCreateData, whose `messages` field is an array). Untransformed,
# the map itself is sent, which the API does not accept, and the Go SDK, whose
# Create takes map[string]any, has no way to send an array at all. Send the
# `messages` array as the body, so every language calls
# create({ messages: [...] }) and the API receives [...].
guide: entity: send_message: path: "/sms/v1": op: create: transform: req: "`reqdata.messages`"
guide: entity: send_message: path: "/sms/v1/messages": op: create: transform: req: "`reqdata.messages`"


